Just to put in a final thought on this:
+3 is unquestionably the correct general recommendation. There are
times when +2 makes sense (e.g. you know you're 2 points of int away
from a key spell being 0% fail, then +2 helm of brilliance is probably
better than +3).

But you want to get people in the habit of doing +3 and only do +2 if
they know the tradeoffs for their particular case.  The reflex should
be +3, only violating it if you have an unusual special case.

So in a guide for newer players I'd list everything at +3 unless it's
an amount of scrolls/potions where 2 makes a ton of sense--e.g. I'd
recommend 2 blessed ?genocide (except for dwarves) since genoing "h"
and "L" is so much more valuable for new players than genoing only L,
but genoing h, L, and ; is not that much more valuable than just h/L as
long as you impress the dangers of eels on people repeatedly
(especially in particular parts of the guide where you address the
Castle, Rodney's tower, Plane of Water, swamps, etc).



